# Hermes Sentinel — Stage H1B-2 external dead-man environment file
# EXAMPLE.
#
# This is a SAFE SYNTHETIC TEMPLATE. An operator copies it to
# /etc/hermes-sentinel/deadman.env (root:root, 0600) and edits it
# locally on the external dead-man host.
#
# This is a systemd EnvironmentFile, NOT a shell profile: values are
# plain KEY=value pairs read by the systemd manager, which supplies
# them to the hermes-sentinel-deadman oneshot process (H1B-2 settings
# loading). Never write `export ...` here, and never pass the bot
# token on a command line (it would land in shell history and process
# listings).
#
# Exactly four configuration variables are required — nothing else:
#
#   HERMES_SENTINEL_DEADMAN_PROBE_URL
#     The FULL public HTTPS heartbeat endpoint URL of the central
#     Sentinel, e.g. https://sentinel.example/v1/heartbeat — the
#     dead-man probes it verbatim (unauthenticated GET, HTTPS only).
#   HERMES_SENTINEL_DEADMAN_STATE_PATH
#     The dead-man state-file path. The packaged default matches the
#     systemd StateDirectory contract; the deployment provisions the
#     directory and its ownership — the runtime never creates parent
#     directories itself.
#   HERMES_SENTINEL_DEADMAN_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN
#     The SEPARATE Stage-H dead-man bot token (never the central
#     Sentinel bot token and never a reporter token).
#   HERMES_SENTINEL_DEADMAN_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID
#     The Telegram chat id the dead-man alerts address (negative ids
#     address groups/supergroups).
#
# The example values below are deliberately synthetic and deliberately
# NON-RUNNABLE:
#   - the endpoint uses the reserved `.invalid` TLD (RFC 2606) and can
#     never resolve to a real server;
#   - the token placeholder `<REPLACE_ME>` is deliberately INVALID
#     under the dead-man token validation, and the chat id
#     placeholder is not a decimal integer, so an accidentally
#     unedited example fails closed BEFORE any network delivery.
# No real token, chat id, server, domain or IP belongs in this file.
#
# Optional variables (leave absent when not needed):
#
#   HERMES_SENTINEL_DEADMAN_TELEGRAM_THREAD_ID
#     Omit entirely to send to a chat without a topic; set locally (in
#     the installed deadman.env copy) to the actual positive
#     topic/thread id. Never commit the real value.
#   HERMES_SENTINEL_DEADMAN_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS
#     Omit to keep the accepted probe default (10.0 s).
#   HERMES_SENTINEL_DEADMAN_TELEGRAM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS
#     Omit to keep the accepted Telegram delivery default (10.0 s).

HERMES_SENTINEL_DEADMAN_PROBE_URL=https://sentinel.invalid/v1/heartbeat
HERMES_SENTINEL_DEADMAN_STATE_PATH=/var/lib/hermes-sentinel/deadman-state.json
HERMES_SENTINEL_DEADMAN_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=<REPLACE_ME>
HERMES_SENTINEL_DEADMAN_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=REPLACE_ME
